From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Manchester <JManch@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 08 Aug 2026 15:33:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] keybinds: consume held modifiers that triggered something else

A release bind whose trigger is a bare modifier key, e.g.

    hl.bind("SUPER + SUPER_L", hl.dsp.exec_cmd("pkill fuzzel || fuzzel"),
            { release = true })

fires on every release of that modifier, even when the modifier was held
down in order to trigger something else. Holding SUPER to run a
`mods = "SUPER"` trackpad gesture, or simply pressing SUPER+Enter, would
launch the release bind's dispatcher as soon as SUPER came back up.

Nothing in the keybind manager tracked whether a held modifier had been
used. CBind::matches() is a pure function of the keys held at the moment
of the event (src/keybinds/Bind.cpp), so at release time the bind sees
only the modifier itself held and returns BIND_MATCH_FULL. The one
existing cancellation primitive, CKeybindManager::shadowBinds(), cannot
help here: it only shadows on BIND_MATCH_FULL, and matches() returns
BIND_MATCH_PARTIAL for any BIND_FLAG_RELEASE bind while pressed == true,
so a release bind can never enter m_shadowed.

The trackpad gesture code had no connection to the keybind manager at
all. It reads the held modifiers via getModsFromAllKBs() to decide
whether a gesture matches, but never reported that it used them.

Add CKeybindManager::consumeHeldModifiers(mask), which walks the pressed
inputs whose key is one of the given modifiers and parks every release
bind triggered by that bare modifier in the input's suppressedBinds list.
processEvent() already consults that list through isSuppressed(), so no
new gating is needed on the release path, and the flags die with the
SPressedInput record when the modifier is physically released.

It is called from two places:

  - invokeBind(), for any bind firing on press that has at least one real
    key of its own. The chordSize() > 0 test is what stops a bind whose
    trigger is itself a bare modifier from consuming itself, so a plain
    tap of SUPER still works. Routing it through invokeBind() rather than
    processEvent() also covers invokeDeferredBinds() and the long-press
    and repeat timers, which invoke binds directly.

  - CTrackpadGestures::gestureUpdate(), both overloads, at the point a
    gesture is selected. Consuming only on a successful match means a
    swipe that matches no configured gesture still leaves the release
    bind armed.

Chord release binds are unaffected: the suppression lands on the
modifier's own SPressedInput, while a bind like `SUPER + K, release` is
triggered by K's record, which is never consumed.

Known limitation: a long_press bind on a bare modifier can still fire
during a trackpad gesture, since the long-press timer checks only
canInvokeNow(). Ordinary key and mouse events already cancel pending
timed binds, so this only applies to gestures.
---
 src/keybinds/Manager.cpp                         | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/keybinds/Manager.hpp                         |  1 +
 src/managers/input/trackpad/TrackpadGestures.cpp |  3 +++
 3 files changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/keybinds/Manager.cpp b/src/keybinds/Manager.cpp
index 9025dbfd..cc7e615a 100644
--- a/src/keybinds/Manager.cpp
+++ b/src/keybinds/Manager.cpp
@@ -583,6 +583,9 @@ SBindResult CKeybindManager::processEvent(const SBindEventContext& context, cons
 }
 
 SBindResult CKeybindManager::invokeBind(const PBind& bind, bool pressed, SPressedInput* pressedInput) {
+    if (pressed && bind->chordSize() > 0)
+        consumeHeldModifiers(bind->modifierMask());
+
     const auto INPUT_KEY    = pressedInput ? std::optional{pressedInput->key} : std::nullopt;
     const auto INPUT_DEVICE = pressedInput ? pressedInput->device.lock() : nullptr;
 
@@ -789,6 +792,26 @@ void CKeybindManager::shadowBinds(const std::optional<SResolvedKey>& excluded, c
     }
 }
 
+// a modifier that was held to trigger something else (a bind, a trackpad gesture) has been used up:
+// it must not go on to fire a release bind whose trigger is that bare modifier.
+void CKeybindManager::consumeHeldModifiers(ModifierMask mask) {
+    if (mask == HL_MODIFIER_NONE)
+        return;
+
+    for (auto& input : m_inputState.pressed()) {
+        if (!input.key.modifier || (mask & *input.key.modifier) == HL_MODIFIER_NONE)
+            continue;
+
+        for (const auto& bind : m_registry.binds()) {
+            if (!bind->hasFlag(BIND_FLAG_RELEASE) || !bind->containsKey(input.key))
+                continue;
+
+            if (std::ranges::none_of(input.suppressedBinds, [&bind](const auto& weak) { return weak.lock() == bind; }))
+                input.suppressedBinds.emplace_back(bind);
+        }
+    }
+}
+
 PBind CKeybindManager::findConflictingBind(xkb_keysym_t keysym, ModifierMask modifiers) const {
     return m_registry.findShortcutConflict(keysym, modifiers, m_xkbTranslationState);
 }
diff --git a/src/keybinds/Manager.hpp b/src/keybinds/Manager.hpp
index 9782a237..c72d2bf3 100644
--- a/src/keybinds/Manager.hpp
+++ b/src/keybinds/Manager.hpp
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ namespace Keybinds {
         void               updateXKBTranslationState();
         PBind              findConflictingBind(xkb_keysym_t keysym, Input::ModifierMask modifiers) const;
         void               shadowBinds(const std::optional<SResolvedKey>& excluded = std::nullopt, const SP<IHID>& excludedDevice = nullptr);
+        void               consumeHeldModifiers(Input::ModifierMask mask);
 
         CRegistry&         registry();
         const CRegistry&   registry() const;
diff --git a/src/managers/input/trackpad/TrackpadGestures.cpp b/src/managers/input/trackpad/TrackpadGestures.cpp
index 2a801541..44dad9ae 100644
--- a/src/managers/input/trackpad/TrackpadGestures.cpp
+++ b/src/managers/input/trackpad/TrackpadGestures.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 #include "../InputManager.hpp"
 #include "../../../config/ConfigValue.hpp"
+#include "../../../keybinds/Manager.hpp"
 #include "../../../protocols/ShortcutsInhibit.hpp"
 
 #include <ranges>
@@ -159,6 +160,7 @@ void CTrackpadGestures::gestureUpdate(const IPointer::SSwipeUpdateEvent& e) {
 
             m_activeGesture     = g;
             g->currentDirection = g->gesture->isDirectionSensitive() ? g->direction : direction;
+            Keybinds::mgr()->consumeHeldModifiers(g->modMask);
             m_activeGesture->gesture->begin({.swipe = &e, .direction = direction, .scale = g->deltaScale});
             break;
         }
@@ -227,6 +229,7 @@ void CTrackpadGestures::gestureUpdate(const IPointer::SPinchUpdateEvent& e) {
 
             m_activeGesture     = g;
             g->currentDirection = g->gesture->isDirectionSensitive() ? g->direction : direction;
+            Keybinds::mgr()->consumeHeldModifiers(g->modMask);
             m_activeGesture->gesture->begin({.pinch = &e, .direction = direction});
             break;
         }
